{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Who is like you among the אלם.</b> Defective in yod — meaning, who is like you among the silent and the still — for there is no silence like yours: they provoke you and you keep silent." "<b>Awesome in praise.</b> Through the abundance of praises spoken of you. For thus we find several things called 'awesome' when they possess one quality that is great in its matter, as it is written: 'that great and awesome wilderness'; 'El of an awesome nation' etc.; 'and his appearance was like an angel of Elohim, very awesome'; 'awesome is he'; 'before the coming of the great and awesome day of HaShem.'" "<b>Working wonder.</b> The custom of the world is that the spirit of the nostrils is hot and melts congealed matter, while the spirit of the mouth is cold and congeals a hot thing — but you, 'by the breath of your nostrils the waters piled up' — like liquid waves you blew with your breath and froze the sea, and the ice and congealed masses melted."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:58:01.074658677Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}